Paradox Codex

Faction Lore
The entities known as the Paradox Faction do not hail from a world, but from a state of being—a dimension where the fundamental laws of causality, identity, and consequence have collapsed into an infinite, self-referential loop. They are not invaders but corrections, manifestations of reality's immune response to existential contradictions. Their composition is a mystery; they appear as crystalline formations that are both solid and ephemeral, warriors of light that cast no shadow, and angels whose touch brings ruin. They operate on a logic that is incomprehensible to linear minds, where helping and harming are the same action viewed from different temporal perspectives. Their goal is not conquest but calibration, weaving a stable timeline from the fraying threads of possibility torn by the war between Lightborne and Void. To witness them is to witness a walking contradiction, a truth that is a lie, a salvation that is damnation, and an angel that has forever fallen.

Faction Warcry
Causality Breach: Once per game, at the start of your opponent's turn, you can declare this ability. Immediately after an enemy unit has finished moving, shooting, or charging, you may select that unit. That unit must immediately take a Battleshock test. If failed, the unit's action fails and it is considered to have not made that move, attack, or charge.

Faction Abilities
Temporal Shift (1 CP): Use at the start of any phase. Choose one friendly PARADOX unit. That unit can immediately make a Normal Move of up to 3 cm. This does not count as Falling Back if it was within Engagement Range.
Fateweave (2 CP): Use when a friendly PARADOX unit is targeted by an attack. Force the attacking player to re-roll one hit roll and one wound roll for that attack.
Paradoxical Charge (1 CP): Use during your Charge phase. Choose a friendly PARADOX unit. Until the end of the turn, that unit can charge even if it Advanced, and you can roll 3D6 for its charge, discarding the lowest result.
Reality Anchor (2 CP): Use during your opponent's Movement phase. Choose one objective marker. Until the start of your next Command phase, that objective is immune to all other rules and abilities.
Echo of the Future (3 CP): Use at the start of your Shooting phase. Choose one friendly PARADOX unit that has already shot. That unit can immediately shoot again.

Faction Blessings (Choose two for your army, one per unit)
Blessing of Chronos: This unit always counts as having Remained Stationary for firing Heavy weapons.
Blessing of Possibility: Once per turn, when this unit is selected to shoot or fight, you can change one of its weapon’s Damage characteristic to D3 for that phase.
Blessing of the Weave: This unit has a 5+ Invulnerable save. Each time a model makes a saving throw of 6+, the attacking unit suffers 1 mortal wound.
Blessing of the Oracle: This unit can never be affected by the Battleshocked condition.
Blessing of the Mender: Once per battle, at the start of your Command phase, this unit can heal D3 wounds.

Keywords
Infantry: Units that move on foot.
Caster: Units that can use Psychic Powers.
Fly: Units that can ignore terrain and other models when moving.
Vehicle: An armored unit with high Toughness and Wounds.
Character: A single model that leads a unit or provides special abilities.
Warlord: The designated leader of your army.
Paradox: The faction keyword for all units in this codex.
Temporal: Units with this keyword can use Paradox Faction abilities.
[PRECISION]: When attacking a unit, you can allocate your attacks to any visible Character model in that unit.

