Warlord's Lore

The Fractured Queen's Lore
She speaks only of unity, of a glorious future where all beings are woven into a single, perfect consciousness within her. She calls this peace. In reality, it is the ultimate entropy—the end of all individual thought, will, and conflict, not through enlightenment but through absolute, horrifying assimilation. Her form shifts and fractures, a beautiful mosaic of a thousand different species she has absorbed into her collective. She is order so absolute it becomes chaos, a single voice so loud it silences all others. She sees the war between Light and Void as a childish squabble between two flawed concepts that must both be consumed and harmonized into her silent, screaming song. She is the most dangerous kind of monster: one that truly believes it is saving you.

The False Oracle's Lore
Her existence is a lie that tells the truth. She speaks prophecies that are technically accurate but morally monstrous, guiding her followers toward a salvation that looks indistinguishable from damnation. She knew the Attack Moon was necessary eons before the Lightborne conceived of it, and she manipulated their greatest minds into believing it was their own invention. She understands that sometimes a great evil must be built to prevent a greater one from being born. She offers visions of hope to her enemies that lead them into perfect ambushes, and she whispers warnings of despair to her allies that spur them to impossible victories. She is the embodiment of the ends justifying the means, a seer who knows that the only way to save the future is to carefully, deliberately poison the present.

The Fallen Angel's Lore
She is the ultimate paradox: a being of breathtaking beauty and compassion whose every action brings inevitable suffering. Her wings are made of solidified starlight, and her voice is a soothing balm to the soul, yet she is the architect of unimaginable pain. She heals her followers by wounding her enemies, and she saves lives by taking them. She fell not from grace, but into a deeper, more terrible understanding of it. She knows that true peace is not the absence of conflict, but a perfect, painful balance where every joy is paid for with an equal measure of sorrow. She fights with a tragic determination, her face often streaked with tears of light as she cuts down her enemies, offering them a silent apology even as she ends their lives. She is an angel who must commit atrocities to prevent a greater evil, forever cursed to bear the weight of her necessary sins. To be saved by her is to be utterly damned, and to be damned by her is to be offered a form of salvation.
